TurboFieldfare is a specialized inference runtime for the Gemma 4 26B-A4B model, engineered to operate within a strict ~2 GB memory footprint on Apple Silicon Macs. The central constraint is the inability to load the full 14.3 GB model into RAM. To circumvent this, the system employs a hybrid memory strategy: it keeps the shared expert weights and FP16 KV cache resident in memory, while streaming only the specific routed experts required for each token from SSD storage.

The runtime architecture divides data handling into resident and streamed components. Metal kernels compute attention and routing decisions using resident weights